>
  <h2>What a lab-grown diamond is</h2>
  <p>A lab-grown diamond is a diamond: a crystal of carbon, grown under carefully controlled conditions instead of deep in the earth. It is cut, polished and graded on the same 4Cs &ndash; cut, colour, clarity and carat. Surat, where we are based, is one of the world's leading centres for diamond cutting and polishing.</p>

  <h2>What we make</h2>
  <p><a href="/solitaire-rings">Certified solitaire rings</a>, cluster rings, eternity bands, stud and drop earrings, pendants, tennis bracelets, necklaces and complete bridal sets. Every piece can be customised in gold karat, diamond quality, shape and design.</p>

  <h2>Reading your certificate</h2>
  <p>Each certificate has a unique report number and lists the diamond's shape, carat weight, colour, clarity and cut, and states that the diamond is laboratory-grown. Some reports also mention the growth method. We walk you through your certificate in simple terms before you buy. Read our guide: <a href="/blog/lab-grown-diamond-jewellery-surat-how-to-read-igi-certificate">How to read an IGI lab-grown diamond report</a>.</p>

  <h2>Certified and hallmarked</h2>
  <p>Our lab-grown diamonds come with certificates from recognised laboratories such as IGI, TGL and EGL where applicable. Gold jewellery is BIS HUID hallmarked.</p>

  <h2>Buying from outside Surat</h2>
  <p>Video calls, NEFT or UPI payment and free insured delivery to major Indian cities. See <a href="/delivery-across-india">Delivery across India</a>, our <a href="/faq">FAQ</a>, or <a href="/visit-us">visit our showroom</a> at Rajhans Ornate Mall, Parle Point.</p>
</InfoPage>
